From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest's modifier keys follow each event's flags (#412)

QEMU pressed a modifier only on a flagsChanged event, by flipping the key's
state, and released both keys of a pair on any input event without its flag.
Typing on another Mac's keyboard through Universal Control, the guest got
Shift down and up in the same millisecond, then the key: Shift+2 typed 2
(issue #412, reported by @ylorn). A flagsChanged that comes twice flips Shift
back up; an event without the flag right after releases it, and nothing
pressed it again for the key.

Now every input event sets each modifier from its flags
(ui/omacvm-modifiers.h): down when the flag is set and the key is up, up when
it is clear, left or right from the NX_DEVICE* bits (events without them: the
key the flagsChanged names). Only a key going down or a modifier changing
presses a key, so a pointer event never does; the same event twice changes
nothing. Command still goes to the guest only while it has the keyboard (and
not the left one with left-command-key=off); Caps Lock as before.

Upstream: upstreamable (upstream's ui/cocoa.m has the same toggle).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-modifier-state.sh (the rules, and with the
patched ui/cocoa.m the wiring); src/tests/e2e/modifier-keys.sh (key events
into a real VM, the guest's keyboard read back; 3.1.8 failed 5 of its 15).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch, before App Nap's.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 #include "ui/omacvm-ime-shift.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-fullpanel.h"
 #include "ui/omacvm-close.h"
